WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.520
IELTS18, published by Cambridge University Press and Assessment, 2023. This recording

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.400
is copyright.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:17.080
Test 1. This is the IELTS listening test. You will hear a number of different recordings

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:22.080
and you will have to answer questions on what you hear. There will be time for you to read

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.240
the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work. All the

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:34.740
recordings will be played once only. The test is in four parts. At the end of the test

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:40.759
you will be given 10 minutes to transfer your answers to an answer sheet.

00:00:40.759 --> 00:00:47.599
Now turn to part 1.

00:00:47.599 --> 00:00:55.279
Part 1. You will hear an interview with a woman who is doing a survey on transport.

00:00:55.279 --> 00:01:23.839
Next you have some time to look at questions 1 to 5.

00:01:23.839 --> 00:01:30.839
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 5.

00:01:54.839 --> 00:02:07.839
So, next, your postcode please.

00:02:07.839 --> 00:02:10.839
Great, thanks. Is that in Wells?

00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:15.839
No, it's actually in Harborne. Wells isn't far from there though.

00:02:15.839 --> 00:02:20.839
I really like that area. My grandmother lived there when I was a kid.

00:02:20.839 --> 00:02:22.839
Yes, it is nice.

00:02:22.839 --> 00:02:28.839
Right, so now I want to ask you some questions about how you travelled here today.

00:02:28.839 --> 00:02:31.839
Did you use public transport?

00:02:31.839 --> 00:02:33.839
Yes, I came by bus.

00:02:33.839 --> 00:02:39.839
OK, and that was today. It's the 24th of April, isn't it?

00:02:39.839 --> 00:02:45.839
Isn't it the 25th? No, actually, you're right.

00:02:46.839 --> 00:02:52.839
And what was the reason for your trip today? I can see you've got some shopping with you.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:59.839
Yes, I did some shopping. But the main reason I came here was to go to the dentist.

00:02:59.839 --> 00:03:03.839
That's not much fun. Hope it was nothing serious.

00:03:03.839 --> 00:03:06.839
No, it was just a check-up. It's fine.

00:03:06.839 --> 00:03:11.839
Good. Do you normally travel by bus into the city centre?

00:03:11.839 --> 00:03:20.839
Yes, I stopped driving in ages ago because parking was so difficult to find. And it costs so much.

00:03:20.839 --> 00:03:21.839
I see.

00:03:21.839 --> 00:03:27.839
The bus is much more convenient too. It only takes about 30 minutes.

00:03:27.839 --> 00:03:30.839
That's good. So where did you start your journey?

00:03:30.839 --> 00:03:34.839
At the bus stop on Claxby Street.

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:39.839
Is that C-L-A-X-B-Y?

00:03:39.839 --> 00:03:41.839
That's right.

00:03:43.839 --> 00:03:50.839
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 6 to 10.

00:04:10.839 --> 00:04:15.839
Now listen and answer questions 6 to 10.

00:04:17.839 --> 00:04:22.839
And how satisfied with the service are you? Do you have any complaints?

00:04:22.839 --> 00:04:28.839
Well, as I said, it's very convenient and quick when it's on time.

00:04:28.839 --> 00:04:34.839
But this morning it was late. Only about 10 minutes, but still.

00:04:35.839 --> 00:04:42.839
Yes, I understand. That's annoying. And what about the timetable? Do you have any comments about that?

00:04:42.839 --> 00:04:47.839
Hmm. I suppose I mainly use the bus during the day.

00:04:47.839 --> 00:04:54.839
But any time I've been in town in the evening, for dinner or at the cinema,

00:04:54.839 --> 00:05:00.839
I've noticed you have to wait a long time for a bus. There aren't that many.

00:05:00.839 --> 00:05:05.839
OK, thanks. So now I'd like to ask you about your car use.

00:05:05.839 --> 00:05:13.839
Well, I have got a car, but I don't use it that often. Mainly just to go to the supermarket.

00:05:13.839 --> 00:05:20.839
But that's about it really. My husband uses it at the weekends to go to the golf club.

00:05:20.839 --> 00:05:22.839
And what about a bicycle?

00:05:22.839 --> 00:05:25.839
I don't actually have one at the moment.

00:05:25.839 --> 00:05:28.839
What about the city bikes you can rent?

00:05:29.839 --> 00:05:31.839
Do you ever use those?

00:05:31.839 --> 00:05:37.839
No, I'm not keen on cycling there because of all the pollution.

00:05:37.839 --> 00:05:42.839
But I would like to get a bike. It would be good to use it to get to work.

00:05:42.839 --> 00:05:44.839
So why haven't you got one now?

00:05:44.839 --> 00:05:51.839
Well, I live in a flat on the second floor and it doesn't have any storage.

00:05:51.839 --> 00:05:55.839
So we'd have to leave it in the hall outside the flat.

00:05:55.839 --> 00:06:00.839
I see. OK, well I think that's all we need from you today.

00:06:25.839 --> 00:06:27.839
Thank you.

00:06:55.839 --> 00:06:57.839
Thank you.

